body:
A bit of context for the reviewer:

My original approach was to patch the `CanvasItem::get_global_transform_with_canvas`:

```cpp
Transform2D CanvasItem::get_global_transform_with_canvas() const {
	ERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Transform2D());
	if (canvas_layer) {
		// Special case for editor preview with follow_viewport enabled
		if (Engine::get_singleton() -> is_editor_hint() && canvas_layer->is_following_viewport()) {
			Transform2D canvas_transform = get_viewport()->get_canvas_transform();			
			Transform2D canvas_layer_transform = canvas_layer->get_transform();
			Transform2D node_transform = get_global_transform();

			// Apply canvas layer scale to node origin
			float scale_factor = canvas_layer->get_follow_viewport_scale();
			Vector2 scaled_origin = node_transform.get_origin() * scale_factor;
			node_transform.set_origin(scaled_origin);

			return canvas_transform * canvas_layer_transform * node_transform;
		}
		return canvas_layer->get_final_transform() * get_global_transform();
	} else if (is_inside_tree()) {
		return get_viewport()->get_canvas_transform() * get_global_transform();
	} else {
		return get_global_transform();
	}
}
```

But after some testing I figured out that we simply don't need to use `get_final_transform` of `canvas_layer`, because CanvasLayer's follow_viewport_scale is already applied at this point (probably at `CanvasLayer::_update_follow_viewport`)

So I simply changed `canvas_layer->get_final_transform()` to `canvas_layer->get_transform()` here.

Another 2 changes are located directly inside the `tile_map_layer_editor.cpp` and they address the way the preview tile is drawn. Original code used transform that didn't take CanvasLayer's scale into account.
